{"at":1795472910191,"value":{"symbol":"DIXON","name":"Dixon Technologies (India) Ltd","screenerId":"1274137","fetchedAt":"2026-11-23T22:28:30.177Z","about":"Dixon Technologies (India) Limited, incorporated in 1993 , is a Electronic Manufacturing Services (EMS) company with operations in the electronic products vertical such as consumer electronics, lighting, home appliance, closed-circuit television cameras (CCTVs), and mobile phones. It also undertakes reverse logistics operations. Besides, it manufactures security surveillance equipment, wearables & audibles, AC-PCBs. Recently, it has entered a JV with Imagine Marketing Private Limited for designing and manufacturing wireless audio solutions in India.","keyPoints":"Business Segments: \na) Mobile & EMS Division (90% in FY26 vs 85% in FY25): \nThe company has emerged as the fastest-growing EMS company by revenue and market capitalisation. It manufactures feature phones, smartphones, IT hardware, Telecom, hearables & wearables. Its key client in this segment includes Samsung. \nb) Consumer Electronics & Appliances (6% in FY26 vs 9% in FY25): \nThe company offers LED TVs (32-98 inches), Smart TVs, Monitors, IFPD Commercial displays, Digital signage PCB & LCM panel assembly, and LED Bar Injection moulding. It is the largest Original Design Manufacturing (OEM & ODM) company in India, and has a 37% share in outsourced manufacturing. Its clients include Xiaomi, Samsung, Hisense, Panasonic, Acer, Toshiba, BPL, Lloyd, VU, Motorola, etc. \nc) Home Appliances (3% in FY26 vs 4% in FY25):  \nThe company is an ODM/OEM in India, manufacturing Semi-Automatic Washing Machines (SAWM) and Fully Automatic Top \nLoad (FATL) models for both domestic and \nglobal markets, holding about 35% market \nshare in SAWM and around 15% in the FATL segment. It offers a product range of 175+ SAWM models and 20+ FATL models. Its \nclientele includes Bosch, Godrej, Voltas\n-Beko, BPL, Sharp, Onida, Reliance, \nFlipkart, Croma, and Lloyd, etc. \nd) Lighting Products (1% in FY26 vs 2% in FY25): \nThe company offers a range of LED products, including lamps, battens, panels, strip and rope lights, downlighters, street and flood lights, and smart lighting solutions, with 2,000+ variants across consumer and professional lighting categories. It is also among the largest ODM players in this space, holding around 25% market share in consumer lighting manufacturing. Its Clients include Signify, Wipro, RR Kabel, Crompton, Havells, Orient, Bajaj and Eveready.","sector":"Consumer Durables","industry":"Consumer Electronics","peers":[{"symbol":"HAVELLS","name":"Havells India"},{"symbol":"PGEL","name":"PG Electroplast"},{"symbol":"IKIO","name":"IKIO Tech"},{"symbol":"ONIDA","name":"Onida Electronics"},{"symbol":"CELLECOR","name":"Cellecor Gadgets"},{"symbol":"543378","name":"CWD"}],"ratios":{"Market Cap":"₹ 81,958 Cr.","Current Price":"₹ 13,390","High / Low":"₹ 15,098 / 9,600","Stock P/E":"52.8","Book Value":"₹ 961","Dividend Yield":"0.07 %","ROCE":"29.2 %","ROE":"25.2 %","Face Value":"₹ 2.00"},"quarters":{"periods":["Sep 2023","Dec 2023","Mar 2024","Jun 2024","Sep 2024","Dec 2024","Mar 2025","Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026","Sep 2026"],"rows":{"Sales":[4943,4818,4658,6580,11534,10454,10293,12836,14855,10672,10511,15548,21794],"YoY Sales growth":[28,100,52,101,133,117,121,95,29,2,2,21,47],"Expenses":[4744,4634,4476,6332,11108,10063,9850,12353,14294,10257,10102,15085,21197],"Operating Profit":[199,184,182,248,426,391,443,482,561,414,408,463,597],"OPM %":[4,3.8,3.9,3.8,3.7,3.7,4.3,3.8,3.8,3.9,3.9,3,2.7],"Other Income":[3,4,19,16,206,10,265,8,497,139,90,537,72],"Interest":[17,22,21,29,38,41,46,33,38,43,24,24,26],"Depreciation":[36,41,51,55,66,75,86,93,96,99,105,107,110],"Profit before tax":[149,126,130,180,529,285,576,366,924,412,370,869,532],"Tax %":[24,23,25,22,22,24,19,23,19,22,19,17,23],"Net Profit":[113,97,97,140,412,216,465,280,746,321,298,718,411],"EPS in Rs":[18.02,16.12,15.91,22.34,65.15,28.5,66.54,